Patch: 018-apply-patch-off
Reason: with the built-ins off, code mode (code_mode_host) still listed Codex's own apply_patch as a nested tool of exec though it has no environment to run in, so every call failed "No usable execution environment is available" (15 dead calls in 7 of 29 benchmark runs). Codex 0.164 has no feature that removes it; its model catalog's apply_patch_tool_type does. The session's machine (host/machine.ts, catalog.ts, written for AgentRun) hands Codex its own bundled catalog with that field null and names it in model_catalog_json; this patch reserves that key, so an app cannot point Codex at another catalog, and corrects the comment that listed apply_patch among code mode's nested tools.
Upstream: ours
Pins: the catalog is read from the session's own binary, in a CODEX_HOME of its own, once per binary; the config key is the harness's
---
diff --git a/packages/harness-codex/src/config.ts b/packages/harness-codex/src/config.ts
index 224e581..2dd8db6 100644
--- a/packages/harness-codex/src/config.ts
+++ b/packages/harness-codex/src/config.ts
@@ -28,8 +28,9 @@ export const BUILTINS_OFF: Record<string, boolean> = {
   computer_use: false,
   in_app_browser: false,
   // Code mode's JavaScript runtime (no Node, no file system, no network): the only way a code-mode model such as luna
-  // calls a tool. Its nested tools are the dynamic tools plus Codex's own apply_patch and MCP resource readers, which
-  // run nothing here (read-only, approvals declined, no MCP server); its sub-agent tools are removed by agents.enabled.
+  // calls a tool. Its nested tools are the dynamic tools plus Codex's own MCP resource readers, which run nothing here
+  // (read-only, approvals declined, no MCP server); its sub-agent tools are removed by agents.enabled, its apply_patch by
+  // the harness's model catalog (catalog.ts).
   code_mode_host: true,
   tool_suggest: false,
   skill_search: false,
@@ -144,10 +145,11 @@ export function codexConfig(options: CodexConfigOptions): Record<string, TomlVal
  * the model (`model`). Also what would swap the binary or shell that does the
  * sandboxing, send traffic outside the log (`otel`, `chatgpt_base_url`), grant
  * permission profiles, keep history or snapshots outside the rollout, or read
- * a file the app names (`RESERVED_CONFIG_SUFFIXES`).
+ * a file the app names (`model_catalog_json`, `RESERVED_CONFIG_SUFFIXES`).
  */
 export const RESERVED_CONFIG_KEYS: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([
   'model',
+  'model_catalog_json',
